// Change: new rule
// Title: Network Capture Via Nmcap.EXE
// Sigma ID: 792eefce-61b7-491f-b86c-1f4e7e6af9dd
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: EinLamYe
// Date: 2026-06-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, discovery, T1040
// Description: Detects execution of Network Monitor's command line capture tool nmcap.exe to sniff network
//   traffic to a capture file. Adversaries abuse this signed utility for network sniffing and
//   credential harvesting without dropping third-party tooling.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate network troubleshooting by administrators using Microsoft Network Monitor
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Nmcap/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/8e7b36a9de00c979a098f16eb29c1c22fb63cb4b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_nmcap_network_capture.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\nmcap.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "NMCap.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/capture" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/network" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/file")
